	<key>readme</key>
	<string># English Sentence Mining

## First-time setup

1. Install the workflow in Alfred.
2. Open Configure Workflow.
3. Paste your Groq API key into `LLM API Key`.
4. Keep the default model `openai/gpt-oss-120b`, or replace it with another model supported by your OpenAI-compatible provider.

Default API settings:

- Base URL: `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1`
- Model: `openai/gpt-oss-120b`

## Daily use

Select an English sentence, run Universal Actions, choose `ew`, then pick the unknown word or phrase. Manual fallback: type `ew &lt;sentence&gt;`.

`ew` shows sentence translation at the top of Alfred results. Typing the first two letters of a word candidate warms its meaning preview. Phrase targets also warm from the first non-stopword prefix, such as `li` for `in light of`. Run `ewtest` to verify the configured API connection.

## Provider switching

This workflow uses the OpenAI-compatible `/chat/completions` API shape. To use another provider, change `LLM Base URL` and `LLM Model` in Configure Workflow.

## Sharing safety

Do not export or publish `config.json` with API keys, or any exported credential variables. Other users should enter their own API key in Configure Workflow.</string>
